---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Visual from '../components/Visual.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { repository } from '../lib';
const tools=(await getCollection('tools')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Base>
<section class="hero section-shell"><div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE · BUILT FOR EVERYDAY USE</div><h1>Your charts.<br/><span>A little more useful.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Underlying market context on your CFD chart. Small browser additions that make the repetitive bits easier. Ten tools for the way you already trade.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/indicators/">Explore indicators <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="/userscripts/">Browse userscripts</a></div><div class="hero-facts"><span><b>04</b> Pine indicators</span><span><b>06</b> Browser tools</span><span><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m4 10 4 4 8-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg> Your existing workflow</span></div></div><div class="hero-art"><div class="floating-chip"><span class="status-dot"></span> CFD CHART <span aria-hidden="true">↔</span> UNDERLYING MARKET</div><Visual kind="overview" capture="A CFD chart with Info, selected percentage levels and the mapped source visible."/><div class="hero-art-note"><span>01 / CONTEXT, WHERE YOU TRADE</span><span>Illustrated workspace</span></div></div></section>
<div class="context-band"><div class="section-shell"><span>Trade the CFD.</span><span>Understand the underlying.</span><span>Keep your own method.</span><a href="/about/">Why these tools exist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
<section class="section-shell section-space" id="indicators"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / INDICATORS</div><h2>Bring the underlying<br/>onto your chart.</h2></div><div><p>Company information, relevant volume and comparable percentage levels. Built in Pine for TradingView, with CFDs in mind.</p><a href="/indicators/" class="text-link">All indicators & setup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><a class="setup-strip" href="/tools/symbol-mapper/"><div class="map-icon" aria-hidden="true">⇄</div><div><span class="mini-label">START HERE · SYMBOL MAPPER</span><h3>Connect the symbols once.</h3><p>Use shared mapping when your indicator needs it. Keep existing local maps and formulas when it does not.</p></div><span class="circle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="tool-grid three">{tools.filter(t=>['info','real-volume','cfd-levels'].includes(t.id)).map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div></section>
<section class="browser-section section-space"><div class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / USERSCRIPTS</div><h2>A browser workspace.<br/>More your own.</h2></div><div><p>Better tab names. A price on hover. A useful question already filled in. Small changes you notice throughout the day.</p><a href="/userscripts/" class="text-link">All browser & broker tools <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="browser-feature"><div><span class="outline-label">TRADINGVIEW WEBSITE · DESKTOP BROWSER</span><h3>The detail you need,<br/>when you need it.</h3><p>Keep the percentage in your watchlist. Hover to see a price. These four enhancements run through a browser userscript manager, not inside TradingView Desktop.</p><a href="/tools/watchlist/" class="button secondary">Explore Watchlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-copy">Edge or Chrome + Tampermonkey is the current workflow.</p></div><Visual kind="watchlist" capture="The same watchlist badge before and during hover, with one ordinary row showing its Last price."/></div><div class="compact-links">{tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='tradingview'&&t.id!=='watchlist').map(t=><a href={`/tools/${t.id}/`}><span>{t.data.label}</span><b>{t.data.name.replace('SVKO TradingView ','')} <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></b><p>{t.data.summary}</p></a>)}</div><div class="broker-teaser"><div><div class="eyebrow">ALSO IN USERSCRIPTS / TRADE NATION</div><h3>From chart shortcuts to your trading archive.</h3></div><div><a href="/tools/trade-nation-hotkeys/">Hotkeys <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/tools/trading-statistics/">Trading Statistics <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-shell section-space"><div class="open-source-panel" data-reveal><div class="source-glyph" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</div><div><div class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE, OPEN TO IMPROVEMENT</div><h2>See what runs.<br/>Help make it better.</h2><p>Read the source, report something that does not work, or propose a change. Each tool links to its code and licence.</p><a class="button primary" href={repository}>Explore on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="source-details"><span>Public source</span><span>Practical documentation</span><span>Issues & pull requests</span><a href="/about/#licences">Licences and attribution ↗</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
